-- METRIC-PLAYBOOKS-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266, BREACH-DOCTOR-1 family METRIC). Owner, 2026-10-24 and 2026-10-26: "FLEET IS NOT SELF-DIAGNOSING ITS OWN BREACHES AND AUTOMATICALLY REMEDIATING".
-- The doctor engine (qnfo-fleet-control breachDoctorTick, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql) ships with four CODE-MERGE/CODE-LOOP playbooks, so its first ticks classified the METRIC-TRIGGER-*, METRIC-REGRESSION-1
-- and METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 family (87 open issues on 2026-10-26 11:20Z) as unclassified. This file adds the playbooks for the parts of that family a rule can prove from ids, counts and enum codes,
-- on top of BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1/2/3 (operator words normalised by two D1 triggers, duplicate and contradicted triggers disabled, breach_causes): it builds only what those left, and every rule was
-- re-measured on live qnfo-audit before it was written (SELECT only, trigger_sql as the engine runs it).
--   MD-1  duplicate open issue per trigger id          0 hits live (the pairs of triggers 354 and 409 recurred and were closed by hand; the owner's note 1000015 is skipped: source owner-chat), supersede to the survivor, the issue that bears the title the evaluator looks up
--   MD-4  recovered but open                           0 hits live (second path of TRIGGER-RECOVERY-1), close with the reading and the streak length
--   MD-6  covered by the parent metric                 4 hits live, 6 once the file has raised the parents: 3 reachable by the doctor (3015, 99914, 99915), 3 closed once by this file (99937, 2570, 100225)
-- WHAT A REPLAY OF THE AUDIT FOUND ALREADY DONE OR WRONG (so it is not built; the reasons are the evidence):
--   MD-2 (operator outside the evaluator set): 0 enabled triggers have one; BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 normalises '>' '>=' '<' '<=' '=' '==' on insert and update (two D1 triggers) and the view reads them.
--   MD-5 (blind metric): the registry already says UNMEASURED for the one blind breach issue (1838, trigger 413); the other NULL readings are metrics with no issue.
--   MD-9 (close deadlock): the contract of issue 2323 passes exactly when the improvement loop's latest state_json no longer lists the finding and the loop still lists it, so the fail verdict is true and not a
--     deadlock; the four METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 contracts are 'deferred' and do not block a close (issue_close_evidence_required only refuses fail, vacuous-probe-result, probe-error and the two probe refusals).
--     Superseding a correct probe to close a live finding would be the move CLOSE-BINDS-TO-PROBE-1 exists to stop. The cause of those issues is the loop judging its own output (MD-8), which is not built either (next entry).
--   MD-8 (the improvement loop files no METRIC-REGRESSION-1 issue for a metric with an enabled trigger of its own; drafted as lever MD-P2, removed after review): its premise, that the METRIC-TRIGGER issue of improvement_rate_7d (trigger 387),
--     fix_hold_rate_30d (388) and open_agent_issues (362) is the work item, is false for 387. v_metric_trigger_state reads val 0.3351 against lt 0.3, hit = 0, and no METRIC-TRIGGER-387 issue exists, while metric_history has the metric at 0.5205
--     on 10-15 and 0.3297 on 10-26 with meets = 0 every day since 10-16 (registry target >= 0.5): the only open issue about that decline is METRIC-REGRESSION-1 100572, and closing it with evidence 'enabled trigger 387' would remove the one early
--     warning and pass its own outcome probe by the issue's absence. qnfo-fleet-control already does the safe version: the covered_by branch of improvementEvaluate (IL-DEFECT-ONLY-1) supersedes a regression issue into an OPEN trigger issue and keeps
--     it open when none is, so 388 (issue 99927) and 362 (issue 1798) are covered today and there is nothing left to build.
--   MD-7, the cap half (tick_sequence_completion_24h written as MIN(1.0, ...) by the D1 trigger tick_driver_roster_tick; drafted as lever MD-P4 on a new migration file, removed after review) for three reasons. (1) Wrong cause: charterTarget reads the bare
--     registry target '1.0' as {op '<=', val 1}, so charterMeets(0.792) is true and charterMeets(1.042) is false, and in metric_history every meets = 0 row of the metric is a 1.042 day (10-14, 10-15, 10-19, 10-21) while the incomplete days (0.792 on
--     10-17, 10-18, 10-26; 0.867 on 10-12) read meets = 1. The ratio is higher-is-better (trigger 4989 is lt 0.9, enabled, and hits today): the defect is the registry target text, and a cap would remove the only red days and leave every real miss
--     green, a formula change that makes a number pass (INTEGRITY-GUARDS-1). (2) No fleet doer: the code loop reads the primary path of a task from main, so a task on a migration file that does not exist yet fails 'read failed: raw read HTTP 404'
--     (ct_im100419 on migrations/2026-10-22-close-channel-required.sql failed so three times and FAIL-SIGNATURE-STOP-1 stopped it; no code task on a migrations/ path has ever merged), and the doer could not read the 6,500 character trigger it would have
--     to rewrite, which fires on every fleet_tick insert. (3) Its outcome probe read the stored trigger text for 'MIN(1', which measures that the formula was edited and not that anything improved. Not built here: the registry target text of
--     tick_sequence_completion_24h ('1.0') and tick_completion_24h ('100'), read as ceilings for higher-is-better ratios, is a data change with its own blast radius (every reader of metric_registry.target) and belongs to its own migration.
--   MD-7 (time-gated 24 h heartbeat metric: tick_completion_24h, tick_slot_coverage_24h, tick_sequence_completion_24h): built in a first draft and removed. Its action wrote a dated record and its verify read that same
--     record, so the engine reached state verified on the doctor's own write and breaches_auto_remediated_24h counted three cases while all three metrics stayed hit: a self-confirming probe, which inflates the metric
--     that grades the doctor. The replay was also partly wrong for tick_sequence_completion_24h (0.792 = 19 of 24 hour slots): of the five incomplete hour groups only 2026-10-26T05 is the fleet_tick gap, the other four
--     (2026-10-25T22 and 2026-10-26T02, T03, T04) are tick_runs rows with step 'pull' ok = 0 ('0 code-task.intake events, 0 queue_pulls rows in 65 min') while the heartbeat was running, so the gap does not explain that
--     metric. A time-gated disposition needs a verify that can fail until the metric reads clear and a replay that explains the whole shortfall; neither is proven, so the three issues (2875, 99936, 2861) stay with
--     their own triggers, and the 'pull' step ok = 0 hours stay on issue 2861.
-- ENGINE: no change to qnfo-fleet-control (the playbooks write issue_triage only, which breachDoctorTick already allows); this file is data only.
-- Every statement of a rule binds the one issue by a top-level id = ?1 (BREACH-DOCTOR-FIX-1, 0.53.0), so MD-6 cannot raise its parent issue: it supersedes into a parent that is already at least as urgent, and this file
-- raises today's parents once (99938 to critical, 100301 to high: the urgency their children carried, including the child 100225 that this file supersedes into 99938), with the previous priorities kept in
-- bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority for the Rollback.
-- NEW TABLE: metric_deps (child metric -> the metric that keeps its meaning, relation names the replay). It holds no work.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE breach_playbooks SET enabled = 0, mode = 'measure' WHERE rule_id IN ('MD-1', 'MD-4', 'MD-6'); UPDATE metric_deps SET active = 0; UPDATE agent_issues SET priority = (SELECT b.priority FROM bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority b WHERE b.id = agent_issues.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority); UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'open', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE status = 'closed' AND id IN (SELECT issue_id FROM issue_triage WHERE rc = 'breach-doctor:MD-6:migration'); UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = 'triaged', close_evidence = NULL WHERE rc = 'breach-doctor:MD-6:migration'; UPDATE code_tasks SET status = 'superseded', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now') WHERE status = 'queued' AND id IN (SELECT 'ct_im' || id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: MD-P%')
-- spof-review: no cron, worker or binding; three playbook rows and one small table on the existing doctor tick. The doctor's second path is the qnfo-cloud-ops watch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1), which files an issue when the doctor tick stalls.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy. Table family +1 (metric_deps), funded by the retirement issue BREACH-DOCTOR-RETIRE-1.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS metric_deps (
  child_metric TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  parent_metric TEXT NOT NULL,
  relation TEXT NOT NULL,
  note TEXT,
  active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'))
);

