INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01QpQv19uh1padRwZ3u1r766',
  'a rule belongs in the doctor only if its trigger_sql names the issues from ids, counts and enum codes, its hits were re-measured live and its verify cannot pass on the doctor''s own write; a rule the audit proposed that the live data refutes (MD-9: the contract is correct and the finding is live) or that BREACH-ONE-MEANING already fixed (MD-2, MD-5) is not built, nor is one whose verify reads its own record (MD-7), nor a lever that closes the only issue about a declining metric (MD-8) or edits a metric''s value so its red days read green (the MD-7 cap); an hour-scale hold is capped at 120 minutes (SLA-120M-1)',
  'METRIC-PLAYBOOKS-1: playbooks MD-1 (duplicate trigger issue, the survivor is the issue that bears the title the evaluator looks up), MD-4 (recovered but open) and MD-6 (covered by the parent metric); metric_deps; a one-time raise of the parents of the covered children (99938 critical, 100301 high) and a one-time close of the stranded issues 99937, 2570 and 100225 (superseded into their parents) and 99949 (MOOT); three lever issues (MD-P1a, MD-P1b, MD-P1c) on qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js with a code-probe each, an outcome contract only where it fails while the defect exists (MD-P1c) and a queued code task ct_im<issue> each as the fleet doer, because intake refuses a BREACH-DOCTOR-1: title for 72 hours after the key shipped',
  'qnfo-audit 2026-10-26: 87 open METRIC-* issues; MD-6 reads 6 candidates once the parents are raised, 3 reachable by the doctor (3015, 99914, 99915) and 3 owned in the engine''s reading by a stale code-task line or a merged task (99937, 2570, 100225 with ct_f1fd327k5oyfkr merged); MD-1 and MD-4 read 0 (the one hit of the first draft, 1000015, is the owner''s note: source owner-chat); MD-7 refuted (self-confirming verify, and 4 of the 5 incomplete tick_sequence hour groups are tick_runs step pull ok = 0, not the fleet_tick gap); the tick_sequence cap refuted (registry target ''1.0'' is read as <=, so the only meets = 0 days are the 1.042 ones and the 0.792 days read meets = 1); MD-8 refuted (trigger 387 hit = 0 with no METRIC-TRIGGER-387 issue, so METRIC-REGRESSION-1 100572 is the only issue about improvement_rate_7d, 0.5205 on 10-15 and 0.3297 on 10-26); CODE-TASK-PREFLIGHT-1 refuses a BREACH-DOCTOR-1: title while fleet_changelog holds the key within 72 h (qnfo-fleet-control 0.52.0-breach-doctor, 2026-10-26T10:21Z); issue_lifecycle gives 166 reopened events in 7 days, 36 of them within 60 minutes of the close, and 57 in 24 h; all anchors occur once in qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js',
  'migration merged; no worker change',
  'issue_triage, agent_issues (close through the close-sync triggers; the priority of three parent issues once, by this file), breach_diagnoses, code_tasks (three queued rows, one per lever); every playbook action is bound to one issue and stores its revert',
  'breach_playbooks.enabled = 0 per rule or ops_config breach_doctor = off; the Rollback header reopens the four issues the file closed once, restores the three priorities from bak_20261026_metric_playbooks_priority and supersedes the queued lever tasks; every applied case carries its revert_sql',
  'the fleet diagnoses and clears the duplicate, covered and recovered METRIC-TRIGGER issues without a session',
  'breaches_auto_remediated_24h >= 3 within 24 h (MD-6: 3015, 99914, 99915; MD-1 and MD-4 read 0 live, so the doctor can reach exactly 3 cases today and more only when the evaluator or the dedupe slips)',
